  "subject": "claims",
  "description": "What was paid against each claim and each of its lines. One CLP per claim, one SVC per service line; BPR02 is every claim's payment added up. The pattern store holds no payments, so each line's is worked out from the terms under \"adjudication\": a claim whose status is listed in denied_statuses pays nothing (CLP02 = 4, CAS CO with denial_reason); any other is paid (CLP02 = 1) its allowed amount, a share of the charge, less the patient's deductible, coinsurance and copay (CAS PR 1, 2, 3, and CLP05), the charge above the allowed amount adjusted as CO 45. Every line balances: its charge less its adjustments is its payment. Claims are under commercial insurance (CLP06 = CI); payer, payee and payee NPI are constants to set for a real trading relationship. A claim for a dependent names the subscriber after the patient (NM1*IL), as X221A1 requires when they differ.",
